# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

data/
data/espn_state.json
# The live-session record (api/live.py's save_session_record). Named
# after whatever DRAFT_DB_PATH points at, so it normally lands under
# data/ and is already covered -- this line is for the case where it
# does not, because the file holds an ESPN draftSecurity token and a
# SWID and must never be committed.
*.live-session.json
.venv/
__pycache__/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# design canvas working files (mockups, not app source)
.design/
auto_refit_daemon.out

# `make deploy-data` output: compressed copies of data/, headed for the
# deployment's volume. Same reason data/ itself is ignored -- these are large,
# regenerated, and one of them is a copy of the encrypted credential store's
# neighbour rather than anything a repository should carry.
deploy/

# Session scratch: SDD ledgers and Claude Code worktrees
.superpowers/
.claude/worktrees/
